## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) >= 18
- [pnpm](https://pnpm.io/) (installed automatically via [corepack](https://nodejs.org/api/corepack.html))
<% if (database === 'postgresql') { %>- [Docker](https://www.docker.com/) (optional, for PostgreSQL)<% } %>

> **Don't have pnpm?** Node.js includes corepack. Run `corepack enable` once, then `pnpm install` will automatically download the correct pnpm version.

### Install Dependencies

```bash
pnpm install
```

### Environment Variables

API env lives in `apps/api/.env` (see `apps/api/.env.example`).

<% if (includeWeb) { %>Web env: `apps/web/.env.local` (see `.env.local.example`).

<% } %><% if (database === 'postgresql') { %>
### Option 1: Run with Docker

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

### Option 2: Run Locally

1. Start PostgreSQL:

```bash
docker compose up -d postgres
```

> **PostgreSQL port:** Docker maps Postgres to **localhost:5433** (`apps/api/.env` `DATABASE_URL`).

2. Apply migrations:

```bash
cd apps/api
pnpm run db:deploy
```

3. Start dev servers from the project root:

```bash
pnpm dev
```
<% } else { %>
### Run Locally

```bash
cd apps/api
pnpm prisma migrate dev
cd ../..
pnpm dev
```
<% } %>

